From d5aeb7cfa0061835c1e6aa6fded6661a749e7e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 08:50:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wallet(v2): authenticate and sign native PSBT slots

Require independently trusted full Coin-v2 records or externally trusted sparse-tree roots and chain context. Review checked per-asset totals, fee floors, locks, selected paths and explicit partial-mode authorization. Use existing BIP340 SigningMessage for supported native direct-key/keyhash policies; preserve proofs/core identity and verify signatures plus ordinary validation before finalization.

Legacy bridge transport is retained, but automated bridge signing/finalization fails closed in this profile implementation. Focused six-flow two-signer signing/keyhash/mode and authentication/proof regression target added; strict source syntax checks pass; normal build/runtime validation pending coordinated compiler slot.
